ped kitchen & spacious dining area – perfect for shared meals and relaxed evenings together.\n\n🏡 Comfortable, well-equipped home: Fast 1000 Mbit/s Wi-Fi, blackout blinds, washing machine, and everything you need for an easy, stress-free stay.\n\n💡 Need local tips? I’m happy to share my favorite spots and insider recommendations for Munich. Looking forward to hosting you!\n\nThe neighborhood\nDiscover Neufahrn, Freising, and Munich!\nNeufahrn bei Freising offers the perfect balance of relaxation and adventure. Stroll through the charming pedestrian zone, enjoy fresh pastries at local bakeries, or unwind by the peaceful Mühlseen lakes. Thrill-seekers will love the nearby indoor skydiving center and glow-in-the-dark mini-golf.\n\nThanks to excellent transport connections, you can reach Munich’s vibrant city center in just 30 minutes by S-Bahn. Explore iconic sights like Marienplatz, the English Garden, Viktualienmarkt, and the world-famous Allianz Arena.\n\nMunich Airport (MUC) is just 10 minutes away – ensuring easy and stress-free travel. Don’t miss a visit to Freising, a beautiful historic town known for its impressive cathedral and the world’s oldest brewery.\n\nAfter a day full of discoveries, return to the calm and comfort of Neufahrn — where you can relax and recharge for your next adventure. Whether you're traveling for business, sightseeing, or a family getaway, you’ll enjoy the best of both worlds!\n\n🚶‍♂️ Convenient Walking Distance\n    • Charming pedestrian zone: 1 min\n    • Fresh bakery: 1 min\n    • Bus stop: 2 min\n    • S-Bahn train station: 5 min\n    • Supermarket: 5 min\n\n🚗 Quick and Easy Access by Car\n    • 24/7 gas station: 2 min\n    • Supermarket: 2 min\n    • Scenic swimming lake: 5 min\n    • Munich Airport (MUC): 10 min\n    • Allianz Arena: 12 min\n    • Munich Central Station (Hauptbahnhof): 25 min\n    • Therme Erding – Europe's largest spa resort: 25 min\n\n🚂 Effortless Access by Public Transport\n    • Munich Airport (MUC): 10 min\n 